      {
        "id": 85058,
        "name": "Amnachaidh",
        "username": "Amnachaidh",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-22T14:20:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Just confirming that bitter strike makes bloody knuckles with a weapon like jack handle in play pretty awesome.&nbsp; DW Fixer can play bloody knuckles, use the jack handle to deal all non-heroe targets 5 damage (plus any outside boosts, eg. Legacy), and then destroy bloody knuckles to satisfy the second clause of bitter strike and not be susceptible to the extra two point of damage for the rest of the round.&nbsp; I want to fight Dawn with him, now, just to cut down citizens. :D</p><p>While the above is an ideal case, bloody knuckles becomes an easy, nearly cost-free, boost if I'm unstanding the rules correctly.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:08:36.490Z",
